0 balance-unequal (Brickwright Robot Lab validation machine)
0 Name: balance-unequal.ldr
0 Author: Brickwright
0 !LDRAW_ORG Unofficial_Model
0 // Unequal balance (Robot Lab validation, test/bw-sim-validation.test.mjs).
0 // A beam 7 stands upright (holes along z, layer z -30..-10); a frictionless pin 3673 joins its top hole
0 // to the centre hole of a beam 15, the lever (layer z -10..10, holes x -140..140).
0 // Left arm: a SPIKE distance sensor (8 g, a large light box) behind the lever, held by friction pins in its
0 // side holes at x = -120 and -80 (its centre at x = -100). Right arm: three beam 9 (3 g each) stacked in front
0 // (z 10..70) at x = 100, pinned lever-beam, beam-beam, beam-beam. The right arm is heavier (9 g + pins vs
0 // 8 g) but much smaller (3 x 64 000 vs 642 000 cubic LDU of collider).
